W: 1 God of the morning, at thy voice
W: The cheerful sun makes haste to rise,
W: And like a giant doth rejoice
W: To run his journey through the skies.
W:
W: 2 O, like the sun may I fulfill
W: The appointed duties of the day;
W: With ready mind and active will,
W: March on, and keep my heavenly way.
W:
W: 3 Lord, thy commands are clean and pure,
W: Enlightening our beclouded eyes;
W: Thy threatenings just, thy promise sure;
W: Thy gospel makes the simple wise.
W:
W: 4 Give me thy counsels for my guide,
W: And then receive me to thy bliss;
W: All my desires and hopes beside
W: Are faint and cold compared with this.</miscellaneous-field>
